  "body": "Found by the independent re-review of PR #286 (continuous C-axis, `Refs #33`).\n\n`cl::text::to_text` (`crates/cl/src/cl/text.rs`, from #279) writes a CL dump without the new optional `Move::rotary` C angle, and `Toolpath::is_prismatic` (`crates/cl/src/cl/path.rs`) ignores it too. Nothing reaches this today: the only caller is `camcraft-motion`'s headless binary, whose face paths never carry `rotary`. But a C-live path written through `to_text` would silently lose its C word.\n\n`TiltedFrame` (`crates/cl/src/cl/frame.rs`) also rebuilds moves with `rotary: None`, which matters only if a tilted setup is ever combined with C-live cuts.\n\nDone means: `to_text`/`from_text` round-trip the C angle (e.g. the app golden writer's `SC` word) or refuse a path that carries one by name; `is_prismatic` returns false for a path with a stated C; `TiltedFrame` either carries `rotary` through or refuses C-live moves by name - each pinned by a test.\n\nPart of #33.\n",
